-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ח/3 — השלמת שעות הלימוד שנגרעו בשל השביתה בחינוך העל-יסודי (20.12.2007)
-- After the 13.12.2007 understandings with the secondary teachers'
-- organisation: the 49 strike days are made up — 27 in planned holidays (a
-- table per sector) and 22 by 20.6.2008 (31.5.2008 for grades 11–12) — and
-- teachers who commit to the whole plan are paid advances for the hours
-- they return.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `השלמת שעות הלימוד שנגרעו בשל השביתה`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date, addressee, greeting, subject line, and the recital of the 13.12.2007 understandings that these instructions carry out; no rule.

-- Time in this file is counted in days from the circular's date, 20.12.2007 (0).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days from the circular to` d IS
    Day d MINUS Day (Date 20 12 2007)

-- daydate numbers the weekdays from Sunday (`Sun`) = 0 to Saturday (`Sat`) = 6.

DECLARE `sector` IS ONE OF
    `Jewish sector`
    `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector`
    `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian`
    `Druze sector`

§§ `1 השלמת שעות הלימוד שנגרעו בשל השביתה`

-- ¶1: the hours to return are counted on each teacher's weekly timetable;
-- §1ב ¶4's example: 21 weekly hours return 21 hours for every week of strike.
@ref akn:art_1/p1 akn:art_1__para_b/p4
GIVEN `weekly timetable hours` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of strike` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours to return` `weekly timetable hours` `weeks of strike` IS
    `weekly timetable hours` TIMES `weeks of strike`

#ASSERT `hours to return` 21 1 EQUALS 21

@desc A strike period as printed: its first and last day and the number of days it is said to total.
DECLARE `strike period` HAS
    `strike from`        IS A DATE
    `strike to`          IS A DATE
    `days it totals`     IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3
`the Jewish and part of the Druze sector's strike` MEANS
    `strike period` (Date 10 10 2007) (Date 5 12 2007) 49

@ref akn:art_1/p4 akn:art_1/p5
`the Arab, Bedouin and part of the Druze sector's strike` MEANS
    `strike period` (Date 17 10 2007) (Date 12 12 2007) 49

-- Days are counted on day serials; a serial's weekday is `Weekday of` it.
GIVEN first IS A NUMBER, last IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `serials from` first `to` last IS
    IF first GREATER THAN last THEN EMPTY
    ELSE first FOLLOWED BY (`serials from` (first PLUS 1) `to` last)

GIVEN from IS A DATE, to IS A DATE, rest IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `school days between` from to rest IS
    count (filter (GIVEN n YIELD NOT elem (`Weekday of` n) rest)
                  (`serials from` (Day from) `to` (Day to)))

-- Each period totals 49 days with one weekly rest day: 57 calendar days, 8 of
-- them the rest day.
GIVEN p IS A `strike period`, rest IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period totals what it says` p rest IF
    `school days between` (p's `strike from`) (p's `strike to`) rest EQUALS p's `days it totals`

#ASSERT `the period totals what it says` `the Jewish and part of the Druze sector's strike` (LIST `Sat`)
#ASSERT `the period totals what it says` `the Arab, Bedouin and part of the Druze sector's strike` (LIST `Fri`)

`days returned in the holidays` MEANS 27
`days returned during the year` MEANS 22
#ASSERT `days returned in the holidays` PLUS `days returned during the year` EQUALS 49

§§ `1א The 27 days in the holidays`

@desc A line of the holiday table: a day or a run of days, with the weekdays the table prints beside it.
DECLARE `holiday line` HAS
    `line from`              IS A DATE
    `line to`                IS A DATE
    `printed first weekday`  IS A NUMBER
    `printed last weekday`   IS A NUMBER

-- §1ב ¶5–44: the holiday days on which the hours are returned, per sector.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b/p5 akn:art_1__para_b/p6 akn:art_1__para_b/p7 akn:art_1__para_b/p8 akn:art_1__para_b/p9 akn:art_1__para_b/p10 akn:art_1__para_b/p11 akn:art_1__para_b/p12 akn:art_1__para_b/p13 akn:art_1__para_b/p14
`the Jewish sector's table` MEANS
    LIST `holiday line` (Date 23 3 2008) (Date 23 3 2008) `Sun` `Sun`,
         `holiday line` (Date 11 4 2008) (Date 11 4 2008) `Fri` `Fri`,
         `holiday line` (Date 13 4 2008) (Date 17 4 2008) `Sun` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 27 4 2008) (Date 27 4 2008) `Sun` `Sun`,
         `holiday line` (Date 10 6 2008) (Date 10 6 2008) `Tue` `Tue`,
         `holiday line` (Date 22 6 2008) (Date 11 7 2008) `Sun` `Fri`

@ref akn:art_1__para_b/p15 akn:art_1__para_b/p16 akn:art_1__para_b/p17 akn:art_1__para_b/p18 akn:art_1__para_b/p19 akn:art_1__para_b/p20 akn:art_1__para_b/p21 akn:art_1__para_b/p22
`the Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector's table` MEANS
    LIST `holiday line` (Date 24 12 2007) (Date 27 12 2007) `Mon` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 30 12 2007) (Date 3 1 2008)   `Sun` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 13 3 2008)  (Date 13 3 2008)  `Sun` `Sun`,
         `holiday line` (Date 24 3 2008)  (Date 27 3 2008)  `Mon` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 22 6 2008)  (Date 7 7 2008)   `Sun` `Tue`

@ref akn:art_1__para_b/p23 akn:art_1__para_b/p24 akn:art_1__para_b/p25 akn:art_1__para_b/p26 akn:art_1__para_b/p27 akn:art_1__para_b/p28 akn:art_1__para_b/p29 akn:art_1__para_b/p30 akn:art_1__para_b/p31 akn:art_1__para_b/p32 akn:art_1__para_b/p33 akn:art_1__para_b/p34 akn:art_1__para_b/p35 akn:art_1__para_b/p36 akn:art_1__para_b/p37 akn:art_1__para_b/p38
`the mixed localities' table` MEANS
    LIST `holiday line` (Date 29 12 2007) (Date 29 12 2007) `Sat` `Sat`,
         `holiday line` (Date 31 12 2007) (Date 31 12 2007) `Mon` `Mon`,
         `holiday line` (Date 2 1 2008)   (Date 2 1 2008)   `Wed` `Wed`,
         `holiday line` (Date 3 1 2008)   (Date 3 1 2008)   `Thu` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 5 1 2008)   (Date 5 1 2008)   `Sat` `Sat`,
         `holiday line` (Date 10 1 2008)  (Date 10 1 2008)  `Thu` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 15 3 2008)  (Date 15 3 2008)  `Sat` `Sat`,
         `holiday line` (Date 17 3 2008)  (Date 17 3 2008)  `Mon` `Mon`,
         `holiday line` (Date 18 3 2008)  (Date 18 3 2008)  `Tue` `Tue`,
         `holiday line` (Date 26 3 2008)  (Date 26 3 2008)  `Wed` `Wed`,
         `holiday line` (Date 27 3 2008)  (Date 27 3 2008)  `Thu` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 29 3 2008)  (Date 29 3 2008)  `Sat` `Sat`,
         `holiday line` (Date 21 6 2008)  (Date 9 7 2008)   `Sat` `Thu`

@ref akn:art_1__para_b/p39 akn:art_1__para_b/p40 akn:art_1__para_b/p41 akn:art_1__para_b/p42 akn:art_1__para_b/p43 akn:art_1__para_b/p44
`the Druze sector's table` MEANS
    LIST `holiday line` (Date 23 12 2007) (Date 4 1 2008)  `Sun` `Fri`,
         `holiday line` (Date 16 3 2008)  (Date 20 3 2008) `Sun` `Thu`,
         `holiday line` (Date 22 6 2008)  (Date 8 7 2008)  `Sun` `Tue`

GIVEN s IS A `sector`
GIVETH A LIST OF `holiday line`
DECIDE `the table of` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `Jewish sector` THEN `the Jewish sector's table`
    WHEN `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector` THEN `the Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector's table`
    WHEN `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian` THEN `the mixed localities' table`
    WHEN `Druze sector` THEN `the Druze sector's table`

GIVEN l IS A `holiday line`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the printed weekdays fit the dates` l IF
        `Weekday of` (l's `line from`) EQUALS l's `printed first weekday`
    AND `Weekday of` (l's `line to`) EQUALS l's `printed last weekday`

GIVEN s IS A `sector`, rest IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days the table lists` s rest IS
    sum (map (GIVEN l YIELD `school days between` (l's `line from`) (l's `line to`) rest) (`the table of` s))

-- §1א: 27 days of the hours missed are returned on the holidays planned for
-- 2007-08, including by putting off the end of the year; they are the days
-- in the table. Teachers of 12th grades whose pupils cannot attend on those
-- days because of the matriculation exams make the hours up during the year
-- "as set out in section 2, and in addition to the number of days stated
-- there" (F-2007-08_tashsach_03-c: §2 states neither; read as §1ב's 22 days).
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN s IS A `sector`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `the holiday days to work` s IS
    concat (map (GIVEN l YIELD map (GIVEN n YIELD Date n)
                                   (`serials from` (Day (l's `line from`)) `to` (Day (l's `line to`))))
                (`the table of` s))

-- The Jewish sector's table is right: every printed weekday fits its date,
-- and with Saturday as the rest day it lists the 27 days.
#ASSERT all `the printed weekdays fit the dates` `the Jewish sector's table`
#ASSERT `days the table lists` `Jewish sector` (LIST `Sat`) EQUALS 27

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_03-a: three printed weekdays do not fit their dates —
-- 13.3.2008 is a Thursday, not a Sunday; 7.7.2008 a Monday, not a Tuesday;
-- 9.7.2008 a Wednesday, not a Thursday.
`the lines whose weekdays do not fit` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN l YIELD NOT `the printed weekdays fit the dates` l)
           (concat (LIST `the Jewish sector's table`, `the Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector's table`,
                         `the mixed localities' table`, `the Druze sector's table`))

`three holiday lines print a weekday their date does not fall on` MEANS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `line to`) `the lines whose weekdays do not fit`
    EQUALS LIST (Date 13 3 2008), (Date 7 7 2008), (Date 9 7 2008)
#ASSERT `three holiday lines print a weekday their date does not fall on`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_03-b: under any weekly rest of one or two days among
-- Friday, Saturday and Sunday, the Arab, mixed and Druze tables do not list
-- the 27 days §1א says they set out.
`the rest-day patterns` MEANS
    LIST (LIST `Fri`), (LIST `Sat`), (LIST `Sun`), (LIST `Fri`, `Sat`), (LIST `Sat`, `Sun`), (LIST `Fri`, `Sun`)

`three sector tables never list 27 days` MEANS
    all (GIVEN s YIELD all (GIVEN rest YIELD NOT `days the table lists` s rest EQUALS `days returned in the holidays`)
                           `the rest-day patterns`)
        (LIST `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector`, `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian`, `Druze sector`)
#ASSERT `three sector tables never list 27 days`

§§ `1ב The other 22 days`

-- §1ב: the remaining 22 days are returned from 1.1.2008 to 20.6.2008 in
-- grades 7–10 and to 31.5.2008 in grades 11–12, as the school management
-- decides in coordination with each teacher; tutoring and matriculation
-- "marathon" hours count.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN `grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for the other 22 days` `grade` IS
    IF `grade` AT LEAST 11 THEN Date 31 5 2008 ELSE Date 20 6 2008

DECLARE `way of returning hours` IS ONE OF
    @ref akn:art_1__para_b/p2
    `a longer school day, in "zero" hours and after the day ends`
    @ref akn:art_1__para_b/p3
    `a sixth school day where the school week is five days`
    `tutoring and matriculation marathon hours`

GIVEN w IS A `way of returning hours`, `days in the school's week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a way the circular offers` w `days in the school's week` IF
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `a sixth school day where the school week is five days` THEN `days in the school's week` EQUALS 5
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 הנחיות ביצוע`

DECLARE `return action` IS ONE OF
    `ask the supervisor for written approval`
    `report the hours not taught` HAS `report` IS A `hours-not-taught report`
    `notify in writing of not returning the other hours`
    `notify the supervisor of the teacher's notice`
    `commit in advance to the whole plan`
    `pay the December advance` HAS `December amount` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the month's advance` HAS `month amount` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct the unearned advance` HAS `deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `prepare and sign the yearly plan`
    `report the teachers who fell short`
    `indemnify the owning bodies`

DECLARE `hours-not-taught report` HAS
    `teacher names`             IS A LIST OF STRING
    `identity numbers`          IS A LIST OF STRING
    `teaching subjects`         IS A LIST OF STRING
    `total hours not taught`    IS A NUMBER

-- §2א.1: a school that held regular lessons during the strike ends the year
-- on Friday 20.6.2008, after the supervisor's written approval.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_1
GIVEN `held regular lessons during the strike` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the supervisor's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ends the year on 20.6.2008` `held regular lessons during the strike` `has the supervisor's written approval` IF
    `held regular lessons during the strike` AND `has the supervisor's written approval`

#ASSERT `Weekday of` (Date 20 6 2008) EQUALS `Fri`

@ref akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the principal asks for approval by 1.1.2008` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `ask the supervisor for written approval`
    WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 1 1 2008)
    LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "§2א.2: the request for written approval is made by 1.1.2008"

-- §2א.3–4: teachers who struck in a school that held lessons make up the lost
-- quota by their weekly timetable on the dates of §1's tables, and those
-- hours are at the school's disposal for marathons, tutoring, enrichment.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_4
DECLARE `use of the returned hours` IS ONE OF
    `learning marathons`
    `tutoring`
    `enrichment`

GIVEN u IS A `use of the returned hours`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school may use the returned hours for` u IF TRUE

-- §2ב: in schools that struck the year ends by sector.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_4
GIVEN s IS A `sector`
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last school day in a school that struck` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `Jewish sector` THEN Date 11 7 2008
    WHEN `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector` THEN Date 8 7 2008
    WHEN `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian` THEN Date 10 7 2008
    WHEN `Druze sector` THEN Date 8 7 2008

-- §2ב prints the weekday of each date, and each fits: Friday, Tuesday,
-- Thursday, Tuesday.
`the weekdays of the last school days` MEANS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD `Weekday of` (`the last school day in a school that struck` s))
        (LIST `Jewish sector`, `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector`,
              `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian`, `Druze sector`)
#ASSERT `the weekdays of the last school days` EQUALS LIST `Fri`, `Tue`, `Thu`, `Tue`

-- §2ג–ה: the principal of a school that struck, employing members of the
-- Teachers' Union who came to work and did not teach, reports to the
-- supervisor — names, identity numbers, subjects and total hours not taught
-- — by Tuesday 1.1.2008; the approved report goes to a special committee.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c akn:art_2__para_d akn:art_2__para_e
GIVEN `school struck` IS A BOOLEAN, `union members came and did not teach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the principal reports the hours not taught` `school struck` `union members came and did not teach` IS
    IF `school struck` AND `union members came and did not teach`
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         MUST  `report the hours not taught` r
               PROVIDED r's `total hours not taught` GREATER THAN 0
                        AND count (r's `teacher names`) EQUALS count (r's `identity numbers`)
         WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 1 1 2008)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "§2ה: the report is submitted to the supervisor by 1.1.2008"
    ELSE FULFILLED

#ASSERT `Weekday of` (Date 1 1 2008) EQUALS `Tue`

§§ `3 תשלום בגין החזר שעות לימוד`

-- akn:art_3 The heading of §3 ("payment for returning the hours missed"); no rule.

@desc A teaching employee's plan to return the strike hours, as far as §3 asks about it.
DECLARE `return plan` HAS
    `committed in advance to the whole plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc §3א: committed in advance to carry out all of §1א and §1ב
    `hours to return under the plan`       IS A NUMBER
    `pay for one returned hour`            IS A NUMBER  @desc the salary for one hour of teaching; an input
    `hours returned`                       IS A NUMBER  @desc hours actually returned by the end of the plan
    `paid by the owning body for strike days` IS A NUMBER @desc §3ו: what the owning body paid for strike days against the Ministry's instructions
    `Hanukkah holiday pay in full`         IS A NUMBER  @desc the full pay for the Hanukkah holiday; an input

-- §3א: pay for the returned hours needs a commitment in advance to the whole plan.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to payment for returned hours` p IF
    p's `committed in advance to the whole plan`

-- §3א ¶2–3: a teacher who cannot return §1ב's hours tells the principal in
-- writing by 1.1.2008 and is not paid for the 22 days; the principal tells
-- the supervisor by 10.1.2008.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a/p2 akn:art_3__para_a/p3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the teacher's notice of not returning` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify in writing of not returning the other hours`
    WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 1 1 2008)
    HENCE PARTY `the school principal`
          MUST  `notify the supervisor of the teacher's notice`
          WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 10 1 2008) MINUS `days from the circular to` (Date 1 1 2008)
          LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "§3א ¶3: the principal tells the supervisor by 10.1.2008"

@ref akn:art_3__para_a/p2
GIVEN `the teacher gave notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days the teacher is not paid for` `the teacher gave notice` IS
    IF `the teacher gave notice` THEN `days returned during the year` ELSE 0

-- §3ב: a teacher who committed to the whole plan gets with December 2007's
-- salary 50% of the pay for the days and hours to be returned, and then, to
-- July 2008, 50% of the pay for each hour returned that month.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b akn:art_3__para_b/p2
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the December advance` p IS
    IF `entitled to payment for returned hours` p
    THEN 50% TIMES p's `pay for one returned hour` TIMES p's `hours to return under the plan`
         MINUS p's `paid by the owning body for strike days`
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:art_3__para_b/p3
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`, `hours returned this month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month's payment` p `hours returned this month` IS
    IF `entitled to payment for returned hours` p
    THEN 50% TIMES p's `pay for one returned hour` TIMES `hours returned this month`
    ELSE 0

-- §3ב ¶4: for pension, social and other contributions the advance is salary
-- that would have been paid but for the strike.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b/p4
`the advance counts as salary for contributions` MEANS TRUE

-- §3ג: the principal prepares each teacher's yearly plan by the personal
-- weekly timetable; the teacher signs it, and agrees in writing that the
-- proportional part of the advance is deducted if the plan is not carried
-- out; the plan goes to the supervisor. ¶2's reporting procedure is to come
-- in a separate circular.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c akn:art_3__para_c/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the yearly plan is prepared and signed` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `prepare and sign the yearly plan`
    HENCE PARTY `the teaching employee`
          MUST `commit in advance to the whole plan`

-- §3ג ¶3: the December advance may be paid before 1.1.2008 to a teacher who
-- signs before the principal a commitment to return all the hours. "עד ליום
-- 10/1/2008" is read as the date of the signature
-- (F-2007-08_tashsach_03-d), not of the return of all the hours, which
-- §1ב runs to June.
@ref akn:art_3__para_c/p3
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the December advance before 1.1.2008` p IS
    IF p's `committed in advance to the whole plan`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MAY   `pay the December advance` amount
               PROVIDED amount AT MOST `the December advance` p
         WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 1 1 2008)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- §3ד: a teacher committed to the whole plan gets the full Hanukkah holiday
-- pay, half with December 2007's salary and half with June 2008's; a partial
-- return earns it in proportion.
@ref akn:art_3__para_d
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Hanukkah holiday pay` p IS
    IF `entitled to payment for returned hours` p
    THEN p's `Hanukkah holiday pay in full`
         TIMES min 1 (p's `hours returned` DIVIDED BY p's `hours to return under the plan`)
    ELSE 0

-- §3ד, the timing: half with December 2007's salary — paid to every teacher
-- who committed, before any day is returned — and the balance with June
-- 2008's. F-2007-08_tashsach_03-e: for a partial return under half the
-- balance is negative, and the circular says nothing of recovering it.
@ref akn:art_3__para_d
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Hanukkah half paid in December 2007` p IS
    IF `entitled to payment for returned hours` p
    THEN 50% TIMES p's `Hanukkah holiday pay in full`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Hanukkah balance paid in June 2008` p IS
    `Hanukkah holiday pay` p MINUS `the Hanukkah half paid in December 2007` p

-- §3ה: for hours not returned, for which an advance was paid, July 2008's
-- salary is reduced; the principal reports the teachers who fell short to
-- the supervisor (identity number, hours due, hours returned, hours not).
@ref akn:art_3__para_e
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the July 2008 reduction` p IS
    IF `entitled to payment for returned hours` p
    THEN 50% TIMES p's `pay for one returned hour`
         TIMES max 0 (p's `hours to return under the plan` MINUS p's `hours returned`)
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:art_3__para_e/p2
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal reports the teacher as short` p IF
    p's `hours returned` LESS THAN p's `hours to return under the plan`

GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the unearned advance is deducted in July 2008` p IS
    IF `the principal reports the teacher as short` p
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `deduct the unearned advance` amount
               PROVIDED amount EQUALS `the July 2008 reduction` p
         WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 31 7 2008)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- §3ו: a teacher whom the owning body paid for strike days against the
-- Ministry's instructions gets as advance only the difference — encoded in
-- `the December advance` by subtracting what was paid. ¶2: the Ministry
-- indemnifies the owning bodies for the advance in its December 2007 payments.
@ref akn:art_3__para_f
GIVEN p IS A `return plan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `advance after strike pay already received` p IS
    max 0 (`the December advance` p)

@ref akn:art_3__para_f/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `return action`
DECIDE `the Ministry indemnifies for the advance` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `indemnify the owning bodies`
    WITHIN `days from the circular to` (Date 31 12 2007)

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Findings and examples`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_03-c: §1א sends 12th-grade teachers to "section 2"
-- for how they make up the days and for "the number of days stated there";
-- §2's clauses state no number of days and say nothing of the 12th grades.
`the day counts §2 states` MEANS EMPTY
`§1א cites a number of days §2 does not state` MEANS null `the day counts §2 states`
#ASSERT `§1א cites a number of days §2 does not state`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_03-d: read as the date of returning ALL the hours,
-- 10.1.2008 falls before §1ב's own last day for the 22 days.
`returning all the hours by 10.1.2008 contradicts §1ב` MEANS
    Date 10 1 2008 LESS THAN `the last day for the other 22 days` 12
#ASSERT `returning all the hours by 10.1.2008 contradicts §1ב`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_03-a, the reading: with the summer run ending on the
-- last school day §2ב sets for the sector (8.7.2008 and 10.7.2008, whose
-- weekdays are the ones the table prints), the Arab and Bedouin table lists
-- 27 days under a Friday–Saturday rest and the mixed localities' table 27
-- under a Friday–Sunday rest.
GIVEN s IS A `sector`
GIVETH A LIST OF `holiday line`
DECIDE `the table with the summer run ending on the last school day` s IS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD
            IF l's `line from` AT LEAST Date 20 6 2008
            THEN `holiday line` (l's `line from`)
                                (`the last school day in a school that struck` s)
                                (l's `printed first weekday`)
                                (l's `printed last weekday`)
            ELSE l)
        (`the table of` s)

GIVEN s IS A `sector`, rest IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days the corrected table lists` s rest IS
    sum (map (GIVEN l YIELD `school days between` (l's `line from`) (l's `line to`) rest)
             (`the table with the summer run ending on the last school day` s))

-- Corrected so, the only line whose printed weekday still does not fit is 13.3.2008.
`corrected, only 13.3.2008 still misfits its weekday` MEANS
    map (GIVEN l YIELD l's `line to`)
        (filter (GIVEN l YIELD NOT `the printed weekdays fit the dates` l)
                (concat (LIST (`the table with the summer run ending on the last school day` `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector`),
                              (`the table with the summer run ending on the last school day` `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian`))))
    EQUALS LIST (Date 13 3 2008)
#ASSERT `corrected, only 13.3.2008 still misfits its weekday`
#ASSERT `days the corrected table lists` `Arab and Bedouin Muslim sector` (LIST `Fri`, `Sat`) EQUALS 27
#ASSERT `days the corrected table lists` `Arab sector in mixed localities, Muslim and Christian` (LIST `Fri`, `Sun`) EQUALS 27
#ASSERT `days the corrected table lists` `Jewish sector` (LIST `Sat`) EQUALS 27

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_03-e: a teacher who committed and returned 40 of 147
-- hours has been paid half the Hanukkah pay in December and is entitled to
-- 40/147 of it; the June balance is negative.
`a teacher who returned 40 hours` MEANS
    `return plan` WITH
        `committed in advance to the whole plan`  IS TRUE
        `hours to return under the plan`         IS 147
        `pay for one returned hour`              IS 100
        `hours returned`                         IS 40
        `paid by the owning body for strike days` IS 0
        `Hanukkah holiday pay in full`           IS 1000

`a partial return under half leaves the Hanukkah balance negative` MEANS
    `the Hanukkah balance paid in June 2008` `a teacher who returned 40 hours` LESS THAN 0
#ASSERT `a partial return under half leaves the Hanukkah balance negative`

-- Examples: 21 weekly hours over a 7-week strike; hour pay 100 and Hanukkah
-- pay 1,000 are placeholders.
`a committed teacher` MEANS
    `return plan` WITH
        `committed in advance to the whole plan`  IS TRUE
        `hours to return under the plan`         IS 147
        `pay for one returned hour`              IS 100
        `hours returned`                         IS 120
        `paid by the owning body for strike days` IS 0
        `Hanukkah holiday pay in full`           IS 1000

`a teacher already paid 2,000 for strike days` MEANS
    `return plan` WITH
        `committed in advance to the whole plan`  IS TRUE
        `hours to return under the plan`         IS 147
        `pay for one returned hour`              IS 100
        `hours returned`                         IS 147
        `paid by the owning body for strike days` IS 2000
        `Hanukkah holiday pay in full`           IS 1000

#ASSERT `hours to return` 21 7 EQUALS 147
#ASSERT `the December advance` `a committed teacher` EQUALS 7350
#ASSERT `the December advance` `a teacher already paid 2,000 for strike days` EQUALS 5350
#ASSERT `the month's payment` `a committed teacher` 20 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the July 2008 reduction` `a committed teacher` EQUALS 1350
#ASSERT `Hanukkah holiday pay` `a teacher already paid 2,000 for strike days` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the last day for the other 22 days` 9 EQUALS Date 20 6 2008
#ASSERT `days the teacher is not paid for` TRUE EQUALS 22

#TRACE `the teacher's notice of not returning` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `notify in writing of not returning the other hours` AT 10
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `notify the supervisor of the teacher's notice` AT 18
#TRACE `the principal asks for approval by 1.1.2008` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `ask the supervisor for written approval` AT 5
#TRACE `the unearned advance is deducted in July 2008` `a committed teacher` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct the unearned advance` 1350 AT 200
